Third-party attribution

Klyndro invokes or interoperates with the following third-party software. No
third-party code is vendored into this repository at milestone M0.

- scrcpy (https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy) — Apache License 2.0.
  Klyndro launches the user's own scrcpy installation as a child process and
  does not bundle, modify, or relicense it. Attribution and distribution
  obligations of scrcpy remain with the scrcpy project and its distributors.
- Android SDK Platform Tools (adb) — Apache License 2.0, Google.
- swift-certificates and swift-crypto (https://github.com/apple) — Apache License 2.0.
  Linked into the macOS app at build time; used to DER-encode the self-signed identity
  certificate and nothing else. No cryptographic primitive is implemented by Klyndro.
- Bouncy Castle (https://www.bouncycastle.org) — Bouncy Castle licence (MIT-style).
  Linked into the Android app to DER-encode the self-signed identity certificate.
